{"name":"Key Lime Pie","hex":"#bfc921","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"key lime pie","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative letter-case form of Key lime pie."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/key_lime_pie"}],"entries":[{"title":"Key lime pie","blocks":[{"text":"Key lime pie is a Floridian dessert pie made with Key lime juice, egg yolks, and sweetened condensed milk. It may be served with no topping, with a meringue topping made from egg whites, or with whipped cream. Traditionally, Key lime pie is made using a graham cracker crust. It may be made with or without baking in a pie crust or without crust. The dish is named after the small Key limes, which are more aromatic than the common Persian limes, and which have yellow juice. The filling in a Key lime pie is yellow because ripe key limes are yellow."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/88/Slice_of_Key_Lime_Pie.jpg/330px-Slice_of_Key_Lime_Pie.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Key_lime_pie","wikidata":"Q1518169"},{"title":"Lime (fruit)","blocks":[{"text":"A lime is the fruit of several species of citrus, most of which are hybrids within the genus Citrus. Limes are generally small, round to oval fruits with green flesh and skin and a distinctly sour taste due to their high citric acid content. They are widely cultivated in tropical and subtropical regions for culinary, medicinal, and ornamental purposes."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8b/Lime_Blossom.jpg/330px-Lime_Blossom.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lime_(fruit)","wikidata":"Q13195"},{"title":"Key Lime Pie (album)","blocks":[{"text":"Key Lime Pie is a 1989 album by Camper Van Beethoven (CVB). It was the band's final album before breaking up in 1990, although the band has reunited and released new material in recent years. It was produced by Dennis Herring, who had also produced the band's previous album, Our Beloved Revolutionary Sweetheart."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/1/1e/Camper_Van_Beethoven_Key_Lime_Pie.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Key_Lime_Pie_(album)","wikidata":"Q6398063"},{"title":"Key lime","blocks":[{"text":"The Key lime, also known as West Indian lime, Mexican lime, or Egyptian lime is a type of lime. While it is treated as a species in botanical classification, it originated as a natural hybrid between Citrus micrantha and Citrus medica (citron)."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/24/Citrus_%C3%97_aurantiifolia_%28Christm.%29_Swingle_%2851906868474%29.jpg/330px-Citrus_%C3%97_aurantiifolia_%28Christm.%29_Swingle_%2851906868474%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Key_lime","wikidata":"Q165354"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/43/Key_lime_%28Citrus_%C3%97_aurantiifolia%29_-_DSC09279.jpg/500px-Key_lime_%28Citrus_%C3%97_aurantiifolia%29_-_DSC09279.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/43/Key_lime_%28Citrus_%C3%97_aurantiifolia%29_-_DSC09279.jpg/1280px-Key_lime_%28Citrus_%C3%97_aurantiifolia%29_-_DSC09279.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/43/Key_lime_%28Citrus_%C3%97_aurantiifolia%29_-_DSC09279.jpg/500px-Key_lime_%28Citrus_%C3%97_aurantiifolia%29_-_DSC09279.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Key limes","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AKey_lime_(Citrus_%C3%97_aurantiifolia)_-_DSC09279.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/